{% comment %}
  Which "side" of the site is the visitor on — the Collect/Buy side or the
  Create/Make side? Bianca's first ask on the wording doc:

    "Is it possible for the buy art or make art button to be highlighted
     depending on what side of the website we are on?"

  ECHOES 'a', 'b' or '' (neither — home, cart, search, account). A snippet's
  own `assign`s do not escape `{% render %}`, so the caller captures the echo:

    {%- capture rb_active -%}
      {%- render 'rb-active-path', a_url: x, b_url: y, a_paths: p, b_paths: q -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign rb_active = rb_active | strip -%}

  Resolution order, most certain first:

  1. The pill's own URL matches the current path exactly.
  2. A product's type — Class and Workshop are the Create side, every other
     product is an artwork and so the Collect side.
  3. A person collection's handle. The catalogue's naming convention is the
     ONLY thing that separates the two person pages: a teacher is `teacher-N`
     or `<name>-1`, an artist is `artist-N` or plain `<name>`, and the same
     person can own one of each (susan-orpen the artist, susan-orpen-1 the
     teacher). `artist-` is tested first because `artist-1` also ends in -1.
     Do NOT switch this to "what is the first product in it" — those two
     collections BOTH hold Susan's class and her paintings, so contents
     cannot tell them apart.
  4. A comma-separated path-fragment list, editable in the theme editor, for
     the pages that hold no products (/pages/artists, /pages/studio, ...).
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign side = ''
  assign here = request.path | downcase
  assign a_here = a_url | default: '' | split: '?' | first | downcase
  assign b_here = b_url | default: '' | split: '?' | first | downcase

  if a_here != '' and here == a_here
    assign side = 'a'
  elsif b_here != '' and here == b_here
    assign side = 'b'
  endif

  if side == '' and template.name == 'product'
    assign ptype = product.type | downcase | strip
    if ptype == 'class' or ptype == 'workshop'
      assign side = 'b'
    elsif ptype != ''
      assign side = 'a'
    endif
  endif

  if side == '' and template.name == 'collection'
    assign ch = collection.handle | downcase
    assign tail = ch | slice: -2, 2
    if ch contains 'artist-'
      assign side = 'a'
    elsif ch contains 'teacher-' or tail == '-1'
      assign side = 'b'
    endif
  endif

  if side == ''
    assign a_list = a_paths | default: '' | strip_newlines | replace: ' ', '' | split: ','
    for frag in a_list
      if frag != '' and here contains frag
        assign side = 'a'
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  if side == ''
    assign b_list = b_paths | default: '' | strip_newlines | replace: ' ', '' | split: ','
    for frag in b_list
      if frag != '' and here contains frag
        assign side = 'b'
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    Anything still unresolved on a collection page is a collection of
    artworks — classes, workshops and teachers were all claimed above — so it
    is the Collect side. This is what catches the named artist pages
    (amara-dube, kerri-sassen, zara-leigh...) without listing all 34.
  endcomment
  if side == '' and template.name == 'collection'
    assign side = 'a'
  endif

  echo side
-%}
